The compiled `langid` helper binary statically links the lingua language model
data from these crates. That data is compiled in at build time and neither
downloaded nor read at run time. (The separate optional fastText model is
downloaded on demand; see below.)

The helper binary also statically links the transitive Rust dependencies listed
in Cargo.lock. Their licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD and Unlicense variants) are
compatible with this project's Apache-2.0 license.

fastText language-identification model (downloaded on demand)
-------------------------------------------------------------

The `langid suite` command can use the official fastText
language-identification model `lid.176.ftz` (938,013 bytes). The model is NOT
shipped with this project and is NOT embedded in the `langid` helper binary.
The Perl wrapper downloads it on first use, verifies size and SHA-256, and
caches it; the CLI takes the path with `--model` (or `LANGID_MODEL_PATH`).

  * Model: lid.176.ftz (fastText binary format version 12, product-quantized)
  * Source: https://dl.fbaipublicfiles.com/fasttext/supervised-models/lid.176.ftz
  * Project: https://fasttext.cc/ (https://github.com/facebookresearch/fastText)
  * Copyright: (c) Facebook, Inc. and the fastText contributors
  * License: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported
    (CC BY-SA 3.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/
  * Full license text: models/LICENSE
  * Download URL, size, SHA-256 and cache details: models/README.md

The downloaded model file is NOT covered by this project's Apache-2.0 license.
It is distributed under CC BY-SA 3.0, which requires attribution. If you
redistribute the model file itself, keep this attribution and comply with the
CC BY-SA 3.0 terms (see models/LICENSE). No model bytes are part of the LangID
source tree, the helper binary or the release archives.

